[{"id":"VRCE-1-45-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":1,"english":"On those sons of her being slain, Diti afflicted with great grief, thus addressed her husband, Marici's son, Kasyapa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.655,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3ee918014b9282f9cc9ecda77009c48039b0ebd8968517044c591cd7086abac2","compact":"ba8126b55f6b5b5ed2de593cad35094e1c45536079897e086ba3d1aed136d138","nasal":"ba8126b55f6b5b5ed2de593cad35094e1c45536079897e086ba3d1aed136d138"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":2,"english":"O adorable one, your high-souled sons have slain mine. I now wish for a son, who, obtained through long austerities, will be able to slay Sakra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"389cb99d5c8c0a84600a2c49cadbafcb945f2bdafdd0ad4a4dbed95596978d81","compact":"59b4e835c72e281f3d11868e33a2178ba1a0e2f9f7db927d79e3921751bd5cac","nasal":"c2d3cf9845addf8484d414023220aa91daf920354fa49d995e14bff74daf94a7"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":3,"english":"I will engage in austerities: it behoves you to grant me such an embryo, such a slayer of Sakra it behoves you to promise me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.705,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8f24835f0d717485ba99327c6ab529d397a70c0f8ad5019d4e89800c4163091e","compact":"0a6e83d7726b63972f0847390553b68731af556039a682eba3042b65b2258f5d","nasal":"44d2bb81818a0b061e38ab11378fd27f7e08fc5144f9fcbf86b1c1da156ae790"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":4,"english":"Hearing those words of hers, Marici's son, Kaśyapa of exceeding energy answered the deeply aggrieved Diti, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9d31857217a0efae761b9d25157c8e1e7b343a14e73bb72eb6bd77c488fa99d7","compact":"105a4e7f92e1036ec8639118cb0a381fa819e052171db8c2aa008876d6bd95b8","nasal":"105a4e7f92e1036ec8639118cb0a381fa819e052171db8c2aa008876d6bd95b8"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":5,"english":"Be it so. Good betide you, do you become pure, O ascetic. If you remain pure, when a full thousand years shall be complete, you will give birth to a son who will slay ſakra in battle.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b4a5aa6ecd9d04496224209a15f71efe3a6cdf6efa9f2371c05d12c802bce0ae","compact":"8deae9475267670756db46565413a364d3971a882845a31b82da731b524a62ba","nasal":"ae48a5dbbfd83204f47ac90e232461acc78cdfe46c476b9b436956537c869387"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":6,"english":"Be it so. Good betide you, do you become pure, O ascetic. If you remain pure, when a full thousand years shall be complete, you will give birth to a son who will slay ſakra in battle.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b594bad17470827815f4974845d1a5ce60116eafcdc985d4f3ad5d789634d80b","compact":"6352e9bc58bb53785e3efbf7f4021d843f98c2a78b58c82925e1c313c358cf72","nasal":"5b64590a963125c8de73764aec61a118e4729c35da2912841f83f6efc8a5efe3"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":7,"english":"And through me, you will give birth to a son that will destroy the three worlds. Having said this, that highly energetic one rubbed her person with his palm. And having rubbed her, he said, 'Luck!' and then went away to carry on austerities.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.524,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3299cc0260199f16040f50d17c37a3b787cda55a1ca2eb999d88e0ca554c1a7f","compact":"f16f1e917e322c547f2e3940128001ef9f9ecb77a4a9d2b819271d90c87dfadc","nasal":"f16f1e917e322c547f2e3940128001ef9f9ecb77a4a9d2b819271d90c87dfadc"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":8,"english":"When he had gone, Diti, O foremost of men, becoming exceedingly delighted, went to, Kuśaplava and began to practise rigid mortifications.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0bb8c9e628547e1fd48f058350c05d693d2dc90bb3b81344d6de789458263bec","compact":"2ad1333ae18a1b8ed6a4e001c0c0a4f37a5e5af803f1d6725375db1259c25cfb","nasal":"74577d723773035aabe88886e6bda908be52bf443724a2d35e4bb46af6b7dc06"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":9,"english":"O foremost of men, as she was practising austerities, the thousand-eyed deity most dutifully ministered to her.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.8,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"35923a5fa354106a8800657e629fcb6e335de3c423c7ffd751f7f274241cb877","compact":"d1f495977d6df1e3a7dbbebf0004f9196d169bf763df4cf90e99c9800bf55160","nasal":"d1f495977d6df1e3a7dbbebf0004f9196d169bf763df4cf90e99c9800bf55160"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":10,"english":"The thousand-eyed one provided for her fire, and Kusa, and faggots, and water, and fruits, and roots, and other things that she wanted.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3695912ea0924e2e7c89e5a5b88b73a23053c969281e8e2e8a9c2687d8cffb6e","compact":"9f0e6eea2183fb981fb09558e615b818a10065960019e4a8a9ab17dacedcf8d1","nasal":"1e8a55c2656f3907b4d35c3b82b638bc9d35573ffcc439f8944997979001f2aa"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":11,"english":"And at all times, Sakra served Diti by rubbing her person, and removing her fatigue.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"adb0aea1df33ffbcfae91499432f9e0a8fee08ed9db66197ea6b536fbe498e99","compact":"f6e0027611892b95156d8be74327af1590078b7ef968eaf7b0c02bf0b2b3b2bf","nasal":"f6e0027611892b95156d8be74327af1590078b7ef968eaf7b0c02bf0b2b3b2bf"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":12,"english":"When ten years only were wanting to complete the thousand years, Diti, O descendant of Raghu, being exceedingly delighted, thus spoke to the thousand-eyed one.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.582,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"62bad7a90ee617f6fdeb3365155a8c1b95fb09d2e15dff55a5fd081431ad8842","compact":"dcde89176b40320b879107cca2d1be7306289222c4e837119396b40cb5dde594","nasal":"cd576ab9110c8b7e90e3eec597038cf334e190487ea5f5a93f92ec8602d5eda6"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":13,"english":"O best of those endowed with prowess, of me engaged in austerities, ten years only remain (to complete the period.) And after that time, good betide you, you will behold your brother.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eaba48c2431f620eebabf3396e16cc4461a1d15ec25b4cd2972e8f561c839767","compact":"2e4324db97f7140f12692322dc747919120dfbec21e0e1fe5347b9030b96d05c","nasal":"17ad02cb9a8f76216fe9b297062dfc0ff899935beb4f23542efe9d6c210dfe35"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":14,"english":"I will, O son, bind him to you in affection, whom I had besought for to compass your destruction, so that, the fever of your heart removed, you will with him enjoy the victory of the three worlds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.866,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2acf331a623bac9c01ec1aa215be130788159491d110cb55f7d2d7ad66e7c40d","compact":"52574b9c55869a09484f301f676145865ae9ab6491030cc0943a2e77e70025ac","nasal":"52574b9c55869a09484f301f676145865ae9ab6491030cc0943a2e77e70025ac"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":15,"english":"And it came to pass that having said this, the sun being in his meridian, the worshipful Diti with her feet placed at that part of the bed which should contain her head, was overpowered by sleep.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.552,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a44b3acaef3113317926e49a28d7770b277ea048075f512b6f738bbf0c42a2fc","compact":"a3724bb4664143999d71986a504cfc39ae1862ade6b077c0c4ce16dab9f85e4b","nasal":"a3724bb4664143999d71986a504cfc39ae1862ade6b077c0c4ce16dab9f85e4b"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":16,"english":"And thereupon seeing her resting her feet at the place where she should place her head, and consequently unclean, Śakra was exceedingly delighted, and smiled.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"51c7109165193ce42a0c47360e3e9c8735e57e546bae6becb7d96b41520feaeb","compact":"c5ac6656a38dfcd5e95ba9acfa2c208ca012c6ff50b03c54a0d7d8f4d4005606","nasal":"c5ac6656a38dfcd5e95ba9acfa2c208ca012c6ff50b03c54a0d7d8f4d4005606"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":17,"english":"O Rāma, Purandara entered into her womb, and that highly self-controlled one served the embryo in seven parts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.404,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0662198b2b74aca88b32d4f10b0d9cb3b2db260eabf37b4f6e0933834d7b5cae","compact":"f0ab2b70b40e5c8e93072f3468bca777cee8c30332682bbf8e255b7a59fb6af9","nasal":"f0ab2b70b40e5c8e93072f3468bca777cee8c30332682bbf8e255b7a59fb6af9"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":18,"english":"And the embryo being pierced by the thunderbold of an hundred knots, cried at the top of its voice, and thereat Diti awoke.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.944,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e9f6f714c6913ba0010c9af7e45d75848d3b75352a15c62d70e58b5afffa0b4e","compact":"77ba616922fbb6f546737c1637c4d0fdb83a642bd67d4d7b3e3834d6743e24b0","nasal":"77ba616922fbb6f546737c1637c4d0fdb83a642bd67d4d7b3e3834d6743e24b0"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":19,"english":"'Do not cry, do not cry,' exclaimed Sakra: and even while it was crying, the mighty-minded Vāsava continued piercing it.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ee8bcfd8b44d9d6ad108126e176419c038babd137214034357231628ebcfe87a","compact":"505932487611b66043b32b22957278c1d806f132484cfdcc806cdb6e422bc7fd","nasal":"e663e10bcf68d4b636bf9e6b84c6e7b3229e9efc2afe627fd9689613fabbd8c0"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-20","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":20,"english":"'Do not slay it; do not slay it' said Diti. Thereupon, in consideration of the honour of his mother, Sakra went out.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.738,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7c0ded3f731f7f992f767c60be9f8585bcbd046583f8d99ce28738c39148181f","compact":"c67462dbc154738ab2518f5fbd648a1efd857f6a7203daefe752a7234df2a680","nasal":"fc3ad291b940f6cefed070f879233e045afcd14f078d38cdc744d2da3d96b6a1"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-21","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":21,"english":"Then he with clasped palms accosted Diti, saying, 'O worshipful one, you did sleep with they feet placed where your head should have lain, and hast therefore become impure. And finding this opportunity, I severed in seven pieces that would-be slayer of mine in battle. Do you, O worshipful one, excuse me.'","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045021","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"697b1e5f8c76c968effee0ac53de7c8b9c68c81e5cc14d9117db8739b6888d09","compact":"733962c30a1a16cada4af37006c4205027801de78a72611d523a16f8eb2ef15b","nasal":"d4c8cc7d1da63f041d01a77e6084d1d6a21981d95b963fa27a2b59a351ecfa96"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-45-22","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":45,"verse":22,"english":"Then he with clasped palms accosted Diti, saying, 'O worshipful one, you did sleep with they feet placed where your head should have lain, and hast therefore become impure. And finding this opportunity, I severed in seven pieces that would-be slayer of mine in battle. Do you, O worshipful one, excuse me.'","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-46-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1045022","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"da597240971d29652636b3c7d7e8e4b17d758784ca40bdbe29a9ac03042b94c8","compact":"49e38abfb7f22e5e529f2e75189e55ef1be7198529846beb6ef865d2340ab841","nasal":"955490e24